The pathogen test result is linked to the tick Occurrence it came from in the `resourceRelationship` table (term:dwc[dwc:resourceID] = `69ae7cfb-cbbd-4fdb-9446-72ddb8be4b4f`, term:dwc[dwc:relatedResourceID] = `SCBI_014.20240508.IXOSCA.N`, term:dwc[dwc:relationshipOfResource] = `pathogen of`).

Further information about the test sample is reported in the `emof` table, linked through term:dwc[dwc:occurrenceID]:

[width="100%",cols="40%,60%",options="header",]
|===
|measurementType |measurementValue
|+Tick Pathogen Sample Condition+ |+OK+
|+Number of Ticks Used for Testing+ |+1+
|+Identifier for DNA sample+ |+SCBI_014.20240508.IXOSCA.N.T.006.DNA+
|+Barcode of a DNA sample+ |+QT00000012943+
|+CQ (Quantification Cycle or Threshold Number) Value+ |+29.84+
|===

At the Event level, each plot visit where ticks were collected reports http://rs.tdwg.org/eco/terms/hasMaterialSamples[`eco:hasMaterialSamples`^] = `true` and http://rs.tdwg.org/eco/terms/materialSampleTypes[`eco:materialSampleTypes`^] = `wholeOrganism` in the `survey` table.
